% =============================================================================
% Single source of truth for publications (website + CV).
%
% Copy each entry's BibTeX verbatim from the venue's official export (arXiv only for arXiv-only
% papers) or from the owner's own BibTeX; formatting edits and the custom fields below are fine
% afterwards. Agents must not write entries without the owner's explicit OK per entry. See AGENTS.md.
%
% Standard fields: title, author, booktitle/journal, year, doi, ...
% Custom fields used by build.py (ignored by regular BibTeX):
%   venue    short venue label shown on the website, e.g. {CVPR}. Year is appended.
%   topic    comma list of: mllm, vlrep, gen, bias, vqa (tabs defined in build.py TOPICS)
%   selected {true} to feature in the "Selected" tab (with thumbnail)
%   thumb    image path for selected papers, e.g. {images/pubs/dvqa.png}
%   arxiv    arXiv id, e.g. {1801.08163}
%   pdf, code, project   URLs (relative paths allowed)
%   award    e.g. {Oral Presentation}
%   equal    1-based author positions with equal contribution, e.g. {1,2,3}
%   workshop {true} for workshop papers
%
% Entry types: @inproceedings = conference, @article = journal,
%              @misc with arxiv = preprint, @phdthesis = thesis
% Keep entries newest first.
% =============================================================================

